## Required maintenance rule

**Always keep this `.codex` file up to date after updates to the codebase.** After changing implementation, configuration, dependencies, tests, data schemas, or project documentation, update the affected sections and add a concise entry under Recent work before finishing the task. Include changes, decisions, checks performed, and any remaining work or limitations. Include the context update in the same commit as the change when committing. Remove stale claims instead of only appending contradictory notes. Do not mark checks as passed unless they were actually run. Do not copy credentials or personal timetable/completion data into this file or Git.

The root `AGENTS.md` repeats this rule so future coding chats discover it automatically. Maintain `README.md` when setup or behaviour changes, and `CHANGELOG.md` plus descriptive commit messages for completed changes. The user explicitly requested Git history with changelogs.

